The above referenced contract is amended or modified as set forth in the following and these
amendments and modifications ofthe plans and specifications are agreed to by the parties. All other
aspects of the original agreement remain unchanged and in full force and effect.
I. Description of Changes
Final completion cannot be achieved until several items on the project are addressed. First, the north
parking utilized Fly Ash to stabilize the subgrade which was saturated. This insured suitable paving
conditions is a timely manner.
Second, the main roof drain coming off the City Municipality
building must be connected to the new storm that was installed in O’Neil.
The last two items
remaining to reach completion on this project are bollards and final landscaping for the north parking
lot. This contract modification will change the contract amount by $86,545.52 for the Civic Center
Commons Project.
II. New Contract Items
The new contract items include Fly Ash, additional work for the north parking lot and to connect
the existing 10” storm drain.
III. Schedule
Through the completion of the project.
